# L §8.4 (tally 2.3, #247; the lead's P9): a comparison of a key-list binding's keys refused names them
# (`w and d0 compared`). Before: an object's address.
=== m.tally
model o_mon
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2019-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
source card "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input w: date
input d0: date
input d1: date
input b0: date
input k: month
input n1: int
input n2: int
input n3: int
input nm1: int
input pay: money PLN
input rate: num
input cal: calendar
input drate[d in days]: num
input mrate[m in months]: num
move pay_x: transfers
  on d0
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay
def cw: date = w
def rr: num = rate at reader
def nb: int = days_between(d0, w)
def ag: int = age(b0, w)
def wk: int = weekday(w)
version v_card
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2019-01-01
  w = window(2026-11-02, 2026-11-09) "c"
  d0 = 2026-10-30 "c"
  d1 = 2026-11-12 "c"
  b0 = 2020-11-05 "c"
  k = 2026-11 "c"
  n1 = 1 "c"
  n2 = 2 "c"
  n3 = 3 "c"
  nm1 = -1 "c"
  pay = 100.00 PLN "c"
  rate = 7 "c"
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], yearly [01-01, 11-11]) "c"
  drate[*] = 3 "c"
  mrate[*] = 2 "c"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2019-01-01 start "c"
ask r62: min(d for d in [d0, w])
ask r62_p20261102: min(d for d in [d0, w]) with w = 2026-11-02
=== expect
r62: refused: RUN-DOMAIN w and d0 compared
  cut 2026-01-01
r62_p20261102: refused: RUN-DOMAIN w and d0 compared
  cut 2026-01-01
warning: WARN-UNREAD def ag is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD def cw is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD def nb is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD def rr is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD def wk is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input cal is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input d1 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input drate is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input k is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input mrate is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input n1 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input n2 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input n3 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input nm1 is read by nothing
